fake08 (jtothebell/fake-08 814991a), its libretro glue and the VM's button
read, on top of fake08-load, -states and -bound-lua:

- Taps lost. Since upstream 6f06d1b a 30 fps cart's loop yields on every
  other retro_run and reads the buttons on the next, so a press that began
  on the yield frame set a "pressed now" the VM never read, and the next
  frame had the button as held only: btnp() missed short taps, and a long
  press came 0.25 s late, by btnp's repeat. setInputState now keeps the
  pressed-now bits until scanInput hands them to the VM.
- btnp()'s repeat lost. A 30 fps cart's _update and its flip() both read
  the buttons in one frame (a 60 fps cart's _update60 and flip() too), and
  Input::SetState counted each held button once a read: the count went up
  two a frame and the repeat landed on the flip()'s read, which the next
  _update overwrote, so a held button repeated once at most (a one-second
  hold: 1 press where PICO-8 gives 6). The VM now reads once a host frame:
  the libretro host counts them (InputState_t.frame), and a host that does
  not (0) reads as before.

Measured with fake08 built for macOS under Diatom's desktop port, a 30 fps
cart counting btnp(4): eight one- and two-frame taps on both frame parities
gave 4 before and 8 after; a one-second hold, 1 before and 6 after.

